California detected avian influenza virus in retail raw milk products on 24 and 27 November, respectively. All products came from the same manufacturer. Authorities have published product lot numbers, required the manufacturer to withdraw and recall the products, and urged consumers to return remaining products immediately and avoid eating them. The United States currently bans interstate sale of unpasteurized raw milk, but intrastate sales remain legal in most states.

The current circulation of H5N1 2.3.4.4b sub-clades in the United States is as follows:
A3: poultry outbreaks in Hawaii;
B3.13: dairy cattle-related outbreaks, poultry outbreaks in Utah, and dairy cattle-related human cases;
D1.1: domestic and wild bird outbreaks and human cases in Washington State (human cases in British Columbia, Canada);
D1.2: domestic and wild bird and swine outbreaks in Oregon.
